# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the Python version is usually managed by the user.
#   For a specific project, you may want to include these files for reproducibility.
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, in case of collaboration, if you are having platform-specific dependencies, it may cause issues.
# Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipenv, see https://python-poetry.org/docs/basic-usage/#commit-your-poetrylock-file-to-version-control
# poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipenv, see https://pdm.fming.dev/#use-pdm-in-a-project
.pdm.toml
.pdm-python
.pdm-build/

